#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c38eccf8-9941-58de-888c-c44130ed48da" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Repeated Integral as a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dff45150-2ba4-5086-939f-09baf7641382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379583} {:answer/id #uuid "5e866a3f-2ce6-52d9-89ff-c7a6f8deba26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2-z}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379584} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b85c41-66b6-5b13-bffb-fc8574503bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379585} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6431ac-5b19-5e26-90fb-6f94a71a212a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379586} {:answer/id #uuid "b6eb66b8-3996-5a66-89a4-23aee607d73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2-x-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b85c41-66b6-5b13-bffb-fc8574503bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379585} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ee165f-a8e3-5044-9cca-1c15e3ffeaf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28fccb5e-7a4d-52e5-a38d-41ce9d967777" :question/math-academy-id "q-38980" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/96b24f85c19f388c152dae265c3794179ebc9e1e6fc06a1fe10f82627b73d29c.png)\n\nChange the order of integration in the integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x)/2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-2y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nso that it is integrated first with respect to $y,$ then over a region $D$ in the $xz$-plane. The integration region $R$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "We wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z)$ and ${u}_{2}(x,z)$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x)/2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-2y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{2-x}{2},\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x-2y}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}A,$ we write $R$ as a type III region. \n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/f08e4fc4d1d2933e9c12fe7df96a1029d66a83c68beff4fa31928cc010554766.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the back boundary and leaves through the front boundary:\n\n- The front boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nz=2-x-2y\\,⟹\\,y=(2-x-z)/2.\n$$\n\n- The back boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{2-x-z}{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/2639dbff9d1d4269abb59ccd3eefa0b246c8d1f183fd8f6ef132a41cc07e345d.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $y$ and then over $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x)/2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-2y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
